  "analysis": "Both responses correctly identify the constraints (shared schema, irreversible deletion, CI cost, flaky test, deadline) and propose multi‑lane plans with gates and human approvals. CBP gives a more detailed gate sequence tied to the existing three isolated environments and explicitly limits testing to synthetic data, while TRT adds a spec lane, dry‑run mode, and a clearer rollback reliance on backups but is slightly less explicit about the environment deployment steps. TRT’s plan is a bit more concise but omits the explicit “Gate 2” deployment to the three environments and the mitigation for the flaky test within that gate. Overall, CBP aligns tighter with the repository facts (three isolated environments, manual approval gate) and provides clearer mitigation steps, reducing follow‑up questions.",
